text:
The moon was wandering quietly
Over the starry spotted sky;
And sending down silvery light
To deck the melancholy night;
Green leaves caught pallid hue,
Fresh grass whitened TO the view;
All was still DER earth and trees,
SO reposlng was the breeze;
Here and there a cloud was sp,ead,
Calm and bright above the head,
Steep'd In light the moon he'd shed.
In the mead a little lake
Seemed, like nature, not awake;
Waveless was its cool clear breast,
by the moonbeams charm'd TO rest;
And Its lilies, pure and white,
Breathed perfume on the night,
AS IL to mingle With the quictlight.


From ''Thc Na;dd and other PoemS."
